<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44317" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭmon</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭmo</span></b> , ōnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συμεών</span> (Heb.
		). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A chief of the Jews</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 5,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Simon Petrus, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				5, 8 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 4, 584</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭmŏnem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1, 423</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Simon Magus, or <i>the sorcerer</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act.
				8, 18 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>An Athenian writer on horsemanship</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 76</span></i> (Jan.
			Semonem).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>A sculptor</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 90</span></i> (scanned Sīmōn,
					<i><span class="en">Prud. Sym. 742</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
